<title>SINGAPORE: UPP crosses 10 mln shares off market.</title>
<headline>UPP crosses 10 mln shares off market.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearly 10 million shares in timber company United Pulp &amp; Paper (UPP) were crossed in an off-market deal in early trade on Thursday, in a move which could be the precursor of a full takeover bid, a dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;This stock has not moved for a long while so you're only buying this if you're interested in it strategically and I think that's what happened,&quot; the dealer with a local firm said. About 9.7 million UPP shares were crossed in the off-market transaction at a price of Singapore $1.58.</p>
<p>UPP stock rose S$0.10 to S$1.73 on the news.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
